From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openworld-kernel <noreply@openworld>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] virtio_balloon: drop clean caches when inflation stalls on
 cached memory

Even with reclaim-allowed balloon allocation, a cache-heavy guest grinds:
each stalled page pays a direct-reclaim scan, referenced/active file pages
survive low-priority reclaim, and large inflates take minutes to drain the
cache.

Add a last-resort, once-per-batch cache drop to fill_balloon(): on the
first allocation failure, drop all clean pagecache and reclaimable slab
system-wide (the equivalent of "echo 3 > /proc/sys/vm/drop_caches") and
retry once before giving up the batch. Only clean data is dropped; dirty
pages are left for writeback as usual.

This needs a callable entry point: add balloon_drop_caches() next to the
drop_caches sysctl handler in fs/drop_caches.c (reusing its static
helpers) and declare it in include/linux/swap.h. No export needed: this
image is built with CONFIG_MODULES unset, so built-in code links directly.

Tradeoff: while the host inflates hard, guest cache is forfeit and
re-reads cost I/O. That is the operator's choice via amount_mib; when the
host deflates, the memory comes back. Revert this hunk to restore
reclaim-only behaviour.

Signed-off-by: openworld-kernel <noreply@openworld>
---
 drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c | 11 +++++++++++
 fs/drop_caches.c                | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 include/linux/swap.h            |  2 ++
 3 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c b/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c
index 123456789013..123456789016 100644
--- a/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c
+++ b/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c
@@ -255,6 +255,17 @@
 		page = balloon_page_alloc();

 		if (!page) {
+			/*
+			 * Aggressive last resort: drop all clean pagecache and
+			 * reclaimable slab system-wide, then retry once. This
+			 * converts cached memory into balloonable memory in one
+			 * shot instead of grinding it out via per-page reclaim.
+			 */
+			balloon_drop_caches();
+			page = balloon_page_alloc();
+		}
+
+		if (!page) {
 			dev_info_ratelimited(&vb->vdev->dev,
 					     "Out of puff! Can't get %u pages\n",
 					     VIRTIO_BALLOON_PAGES_PER_PAGE);
diff --git a/fs/drop_caches.c b/fs/drop_caches.c
index 123456789017..123456789018 100644
--- a/fs/drop_caches.c
+++ b/fs/drop_caches.c
@@ -48,6 +48,23 @@
 	iput(toput_inode);
 }

+/*
+ * balloon_drop_caches - drop all clean pagecache and reclaimable slab,
+ *			 for memory ballooning.
+ *
+ * Same as "echo 3 > /proc/sys/vm/drop_caches" but callable from the
+ * balloon driver when inflation stalls on cached memory. Only clean data
+ * is dropped; dirty pages are left for writeback as usual.
+ */
+void balloon_drop_caches(void)
+{
+	lru_add_drain_all();
+	iterate_supers(drop_pagecache_sb, NULL);
+	count_vm_event(DROP_PAGECACHE);
+	drop_slab();
+	count_vm_event(DROP_SLAB);
+}
+
 static int drop_caches_sysctl_handler(const struct ctl_table *table, int write,
 		void *buffer, size_t *length, loff_t *ppos)
 {
diff --git a/include/linux/swap.h b/include/linux/swap.h
index 123456789019..123456789020 100644
--- a/include/linux/swap.h
+++ b/include/linux/swap.h
@@ -401,6 +401,8 @@
 						pg_data_t *pgdat,
 						unsigned long *nr_scanned);
 extern unsigned long shrink_all_memory(unsigned long nr_pages);
+/* Drop clean pagecache and reclaimable slab (for balloon inflation). */
+void balloon_drop_caches(void);
 extern int vm_swappiness;
 long remove_mapping(struct address_space *mapping, struct folio *folio);

--
2.47.0
